    {
      "id": "attribution",
      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Original rotating-camera controls - MIT",
      "description": "Original MIT environment texture, pinhole captures, generator, projects and known landmarks by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors. No customer or third-party images. Known camera focal 420 pixels on 480x360 views; yaw -36, 0, +36 degrees. Left/right have no direct overlap; center connects them even when input order puts the disconnected pair first. Native camera fitting is independently checked against feature homographies. Coverage excludes unobserved pixels. Point markers map source corners into the new panorama frame. Disconnected/distorted examples fail normally; partial policies are explicit. Diagnostics use a separate grid. These camera estimates are for panorama fitting, not physical metrology, lens calibration or robot extrinsics. See README/truth.json for numerical tolerances.",
      "parameters": {},
      "position": [
        0,
        -650
